/F1 8.5 Tf
12.5 TL
(   [Problem Statement]: Explain Pointer Fundamentals in C, detailing address-of \(&\) and indirection \(*\) operators, pointer sizing, and physical memory addressing.) Tj
T*
(   [Detailed Step-by-Step Answer]:) Tj
T*
(   Pointer Fundamentals and Architecture in C:) Tj
T*
(   1. Definition and Physical Architecture:) Tj
T*
(   - A pointer is a variable whose stored value is the physical or virtual memory address of) Tj
T*
(   another variable.) Tj
T*
(   - Pointers provide direct access to microprocessor memory registers and system RAM.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(   2. Fundamental Operators:) Tj
T*
(   - Address-Of Operator \(&\): Unary operator that returns the memory address of an lvalue operand.) Tj
T*
(   int x = 42;) Tj
T*
(   int *ptr = &x; /* ptr receives address of x \(e.g., 0x7ffd10\) */) Tj
T*
(   - Indirection / Dereferencing Operator \(*\): Accesses or mutates the value located at the) Tj
T*
(   address held by the pointer.) Tj
T*
(   *ptr = 99; /* Writes 99 directly into variable x's memory */) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(   3. Uniform Pointer Sizing:) Tj
T*
(   - Rule: Regardless of the data type pointed to \(char, int, double, struct\), a pointer variable) Tj
T*
(   ALWAYS occupies the exact same memory width required to hold an architecture address!) Tj
T*
(   - 32-bit Architecture \(x86\): 32-bit address bus -> sizeof\(any_pointer\) = 4 bytes.) Tj
T*
(   - 64-bit Architecture \(x86-64\): 64-bit address bus -> sizeof\(any_pointer\) = 8 bytes.) Tj
T*
(   - sizeof\(char*\) == sizeof\(int*\) == sizeof\(double*\) == sizeof\(void*\) == 8 bytes \(on 64-bit\).) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(   4. Complete ANSI C Demonstration Program:) Tj
T*
(   #include <stdio.h>) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(   int main\(void\) {) Tj
T*
(   char c = 'A';) Tj
T*
(   int i = 100;) Tj
T*
(   double d = 3.14159;) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(   char *pc = &c;) Tj
T*
(   int *pi = &i;) Tj
T*
(   double *pd = &d;) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(   printf\("=== Memory Footprint of Pointers \(64-bit ABI\) ===\\n"\);) Tj
T*
(   printf\("sizeof\(char*\): %zu bytes | Points to %zu-byte char at %p\\n", sizeof\(pc\), sizeof\(*pc\),) Tj
T*
(   \(void *\)pc\);) Tj
T*
(   printf\("sizeof\(int*\): %zu bytes | Points to %zu-byte int at %p\\n", sizeof\(pi\), sizeof\(*pi\),) Tj
T*
(   \(void *\)pi\);) Tj
T*
(   printf\("sizeof\(double*\): %zu bytes | Points to %zu-byte double at %p\\n", sizeof\(pd\),) Tj
T*
(   sizeof\(*pd\), \(void *\)pd\);) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(   /* Dereferencing mutation */) Tj
T*
(   *pi = 500;) Tj
T*
(   printf\("Value of integer 'i' after pointer mutation: %d\\n", i\);) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(   return 0;) Tj
T*
(   }) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
ET

