12.5 TL
(   [Problem Statement]: Explain Pointer Classification: Wild Pointers, NULL Pointers, Dangling Pointers, and Void Pointers with prevention strategies.) Tj
T*
(   [Detailed Step-by-Step Answer]:) Tj
T*
(   Classification of Pointers in C:) Tj
T*
(   1. Wild Pointer:) Tj
T*
(   - Definition: A pointer variable that has been declared but never initialized.) Tj
T*
(   int *p; /* Uninitialized: contains random stack garbage bits */) Tj
T*
(   - Hazard: Dereferencing *p accesses arbitrary memory addresses, causing immediate segmentation) Tj
T*
(   faults or corrupting unrelated variables.) Tj
T*
(   - Prevention: Always initialize pointers upon declaration: int *p = NULL;) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
ET

