BT
/F1 8.5 Tf
12.5 TL
45 780 Td
(   2. NULL Pointer:) Tj
T*
(   - Definition: A pointer explicitly assigned the constant value NULL \(\(void*\)0\).) Tj
T*
(   - Guarantee: Standard guarantees NULL points to an invalid address that cannot be dereferenced) Tj
T*
(   by any user program.) Tj
T*
(   - Purpose: Serves as a defensive sentinel indicating 'points to nothing' or 'allocation) Tj
T*
(   failed'.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(   3. Dangling Pointer:) Tj
T*
(   - Definition: A pointer that continues referencing a memory location after the storage has been) Tj
T*
(   released or destroyed.) Tj
T*
(   Occurs when:) Tj
T*
(   a. Calling free\(ptr\) without resetting ptr to NULL.) Tj
T*
(   b. Returning the address of a local stack variable from a function.) Tj
T*
(   - Hazard: 'Use-After-Free' security exploit. Memory may be reallocated to another process) Tj
T*
(   component; reading/writing it causes severe data corruption.) Tj
T*
(   - Prevention: Immediately set pointer to NULL after freeing: free\(p\); p = NULL;) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(   4. Void Pointer \(Generic Pointer void*\):) Tj
T*
(   - Definition: A pointer that represents a raw memory address without any associated data type.) Tj
T*
(   - Properties: Can hold address of any type \(int*, double*, struct*\).) Tj
T*
(   - Dereference Restriction: CANNOT be dereferenced directly without explicit casting: *\(int*\)vp.) Tj
T*
(   - Arithmetic Restriction: Standard C forbids pointer arithmetic on void* \(since sizeof\(void\) is) Tj
T*
(   incomplete\). Used extensively in malloc, qsort, and memcpy.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(--------------------------------------------------------------------------------) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
