(   [Problem Statement]: Detail Dynamic Memory Allocation functions: malloc\(\), calloc\(\), realloc\(\), and free\(\), explaining heap internals and failure handling.) Tj
T*
(   [Detailed Step-by-Step Answer]:) Tj
T*
(   Dynamic Memory Allocation Architecture in C:) Tj
T*
(   1. Heap Memory Segment:) Tj
T*
(   Dynamic memory is allocated on the Heap, an unorganized pool of memory managed by the operating) Tj
T*
(   system kernel and runtime allocator \(ptmalloc, jemalloc\). Memory persists until explicitly) Tj
T*
(   deallocated.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(   2. Allocation Functions Breakdown:) Tj
T*
(   a. malloc\(size_t size\):) Tj
T*
(   - Allocates 'size' contiguous bytes of uninitialized memory.) Tj
T*
(   - Returns void* pointer to base address, or NULL on allocation failure.) Tj
T*
(   - Data contains indeterminate garbage bits.) Tj
T*
(   b. calloc\(size_t num, size_t size\):) Tj
T*
(   - Allocates contiguous array of 'num' elements of 'size' bytes each.) Tj
T*
(   - Guarantees ALL bytes are initialized to zero \(0\).) Tj
T*
(   - Prevents integer overflow: checks if num * size wraps around.) Tj
T*
(   c. realloc\(void *ptr, size_t new_size\):) Tj
T*
(   - Resizes previously allocated block.) Tj
T*
(   - If possible, expands block in-place. If contiguous space is blocked, allocates a new block) Tj
T*
(   elsewhere, copies existing bytes, frees old block, and returns new address.) Tj
T*
(   - Critical Rule: If realloc fails, it returns NULL BUT LEAVES ORIGINAL BLOCK INTACT!) Tj
T*
(   d. free\(void *ptr\):) Tj
T*
(   - Returns heap block to allocator free list. Passing NULL is safe \(no-op\).) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(   3. Complete Defensive Allocation Program:) Tj
T*
(   #include <stdio.h>) Tj
T*
(   #include <stdlib.h>) Tj
T*
ET

