(   [Problem Statement]: Write an ANSI C program to allocate, populate, and deallocate a dynamic 2D array \(matrix\) using pointers to pointers \(int **\).) Tj
T*
(   [Detailed Step-by-Step Answer]:) Tj
T*
(   Dynamic 2D Array Allocation Using Double Pointers:) Tj
T*
(   1. Structural Concept:) Tj
T*
(   A dynamic 2D array can be structured as an array of pointers \(rows\), where each pointer) Tj
T*
(   addresses an independently allocated 1D array of elements \(columns\).) Tj
T*
(   - mat: Pointer to pointer \(int **\).) Tj
T*
(   - mat[i]: Pointer to row 'i' \(int *\).) Tj
T*
(   - mat[i][j]: The actual integer element at row i, col j \(*\(*\(mat + i\) + j\)\).) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(   2. Step-by-Step Allocation Algorithm:) Tj
T*
(   Step 1: Allocate array of row pointers:) Tj
T*
(   mat = \(int **\)malloc\(rows * sizeof\(int *\)\);) Tj
T*
(   Step 2: For each row i, allocate column buffer:) Tj
T*
(   mat[i] = \(int *\)malloc\(cols * sizeof\(int\)\);) Tj
T*
