(   [Problem Statement]: Explain Strings in C, contrasting string literals vs character arrays, null termination \('\\0'\), and string literal immutability.) Tj
T*
(   [Detailed Step-by-Step Answer]:) Tj
T*
(   Strings in C: Representation, Storage, and Immutability:) Tj
T*
(   1. Language Definition:) Tj
T*
(   In ANSI C, there is NO primitive 'string' data type.) Tj
T*
(   A string is formally defined as a contiguous array of characters terminated by a null character) Tj
T*
(   \('\\0', byte value 0\).) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(   2. String Literals vs Character Arrays:) Tj
T*
(   - String Literal: char *str = "Biotech";) Tj
T*
(   - Storage Location: Read-Only Data Segment \(.rodata / Text segment\).) Tj
T*
(   - Immutability: Memory is marked read-only by the OS MMU.) Tj
T*
(   - Attempting to modify str[0] = 'b'; triggers a segmentation fault \(SIGSEGV\)!) Tj
T*
(   - Character Array: char arr[] = "Biotech";) Tj
T*
(   - Storage Location: Stack Frame \(or Data segment if global\).) Tj
T*
(   - Initialization: The compiler allocates an 8-byte array on the stack and copies the characters) Tj
T*
(   'B','i','o','t','e','c','h','\\0' into it.) Tj
T*
(   - Mutability: Fully mutable! arr[0] = 'b'; executes safely.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(   3. The Role of the Null Terminator \('\\0'\):) Tj
T*
(   Because character arrays carry no length metadata, all standard string processing functions) Tj
T*
(   \(strlen, strcpy, printf %s\) iterate sequentially until encountering '\\0'.) Tj
T*
(   If a string buffer lacks '\\0', functions run off the end into unallocated memory, causing) Tj
T*
(   buffer overflows or crashes.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(   4. Demonstrative ANSI C Program:) Tj
T*
(   #include <stdio.h>) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(   int main\(void\) {) Tj
T*
(   /* Mutable Stack Array */) Tj
T*
(   char sequence_array[] = "ATGC";) Tj
T*
(   sequence_array[0] = 'C'; /* Completely legal */) Tj
T*
(   printf\("Modified stack string: %s \(Length: 4\)\\n", sequence_array\);) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(   /* Immutable String Literal */) Tj
T*
(   const char *sequence_literal = "ATGC";) Tj
T*
(   printf\("Read-only literal at %p: %s\\n", \(void *\)sequence_literal, sequence_literal\);) Tj
T*
(   /* sequence_literal[0] = 'C'; -> Triggers runtime hardware fault! */) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(   return 0;) Tj
T*
(   }) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(--------------------------------------------------------------------------------) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
ET
