(   The Four Critical Heap Memory Vulnerabilities in C:) Tj
T*
(   1. Memory Leak:) Tj
T*
(   - Cause: Allocating heap memory via malloc/calloc and allowing all pointers referencing that) Tj
T*
(   block to be overwritten or fall out of scope without calling free\(\).) Tj
T*
(   - Consequence: Heap memory grows monotonically, exhausting physical RAM and swap space,) Tj
T*
(   resulting in Out-Of-Memory \(OOM\) kernel panics.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(   2. Double-Free Vulnerability:) Tj
T*
(   - Cause: Invoking free\(ptr\) twice on the exact same heap memory pointer without an intervening) Tj
T*
(   allocation.) Tj
T*
(   - Consequence: Corrupts the heap allocator's internal free-list bin metadata \(fastbins /) Tj
T*
(   tcache\), enabling arbitrary code execution exploits.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(   3. Use-After-Free \(UAF\):) Tj
T*
(   - Cause: Accessing memory through a pointer after calling free\(ptr\).) Tj
T*
(   - Consequence: The deallocated memory may be reallocated to another object. Modifying the old) Tj
T*
(   pointer corrupts the new object's data or vtable pointers.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(   4. Heap Buffer Overflow:) Tj
T*
(   - Cause: Writing more bytes into a dynamically allocated buffer than the requested allocation) Tj
T*
(   size.) Tj
T*
(   - Consequence: Overwrites heap metadata chunks and adjacent allocated objects, destroying heap) Tj
T*
(   consistency.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(   5. Prevention Best-Practice Code:) Tj
T*
(   #include <stdio.h>) Tj
T*
(   #include <stdlib.h>) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(   void safe_deallocate\(void **ptr_ref\) {) Tj
T*
(   if \(ptr_ref != NULL && *ptr_ref != NULL\) {) Tj
T*
(   free\(*ptr_ref\);) Tj
T*
(   *ptr_ref = NULL; /* Nullifies dangling pointer */) Tj
T*
(   }) Tj
T*
(   }) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(   int main\(void\) {) Tj
T*
(   int *buffer = \(int *\)malloc\(10 * sizeof\(int\)\);) Tj
T*
(   /* Safe deallocation macro / wrapper */) Tj
T*
(   safe_deallocate\(\(void **\)&buffer\);) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(   /* Second free is now completely safe \(free\(NULL\) is no-op\) */) Tj
T*
(   safe_deallocate\(\(void **\)&buffer\);) Tj
T*
(   printf\("Safely avoided double-free and dangling pointer traps.\\n"\);) Tj
T*
(   return 0;) Tj
T*
(   }) Tj
T*
() Tj
