(   [Problem Statement]: Explain memory layout of a compiled C program: Text, Data, BSS, Heap, and Stack segments with virtual address directionality.) Tj
T*
(   [Detailed Step-by-Step Answer]:) Tj
T*
(   Memory Layout of a C Program:) Tj
T*
(   Modern operating systems present each C process with a unified Virtual Address Space) Tj
T*
(   partitioned into five distinct segments:) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(   1. Text Segment \(Code Segment\):) Tj
T*
(   - Stores machine instructions compiled from C code.) Tj
T*
(   - Read-only and shareable across concurrent process instances. Prevents self-modifying code) Tj
T*
(   vulnerabilities.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(   2. Initialized Data Segment \(.data\):) Tj
T*
(   - Stores global and static variables explicitly initialized to non-zero values by the) Tj
T*
(   programmer:) Tj
T*
(   int global_cycles = 42;) Tj
T*
(   static double threshold = 0.05;) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(   3. Uninitialized Data Segment \(.bss - Block Started by Symbol\):) Tj
T*
(   - Stores global and static variables that are uninitialized or initialized to zero.) Tj
T*
(   - Takes zero bytes in the disk executable file \(OS kernel zero-fills this segment at process) Tj
T*
(   startup\).) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(   4. Heap Segment:) Tj
T*
(   - Manages dynamically allocated memory \(malloc, calloc, realloc\).) Tj
T*
(   - Grows UPWARD from lower to higher memory addresses as memory is requested \(managed via) Tj
T*
(   brk/sbrk and mmap\).) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(   5. Call Stack Segment:) Tj
T*
(   - Manages automatic local variables, function parameters, stack frames, and return addresses.) Tj
T*
(   - Grows DOWNWARD from higher to lower memory addresses.) Tj
T*
(   - Stack Overflow occurs when the downward-growing Stack collides with the upward-growing Heap!) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(   Visual Diagram:) Tj
T*
(   [High Address 0x7FFF...]) Tj
T*
(   | Call Stack \(grows DOWNWARD\) |) Tj
T*
(   | v |) Tj
T*
(   | ^ |) Tj
T*
(   | Heap \(grows UPWARD\) |) Tj
T*
(   | BSS Segment \(Zero-filled\) |) Tj
T*
(   | Data Segment \(.data\) |) Tj
T*
(   | Text Segment \(.text / Code\) |) Tj
T*
(   [Low Address 0x0040...]) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(--------------------------------------------------------------------------------) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
