(   [Problem Statement]: Write an ANSI C program to sort an array of strings alphabetically using qsort\(\) and pointer comparison callbacks.) Tj
T*
(   [Detailed Step-by-Step Answer]:) Tj
T*
(   Alphabetical String Array Sorting with qsort\(\):) Tj
T*
(   1. Double Indirection in String Comparators:) Tj
T*
(   When sorting an array of strings \(char *arr[]\), qsort passes pointers to array elements into) Tj
T*
(   the comparator callback.) Tj
T*
(   Since the array elements are themselves pointers \(char*\), the arguments passed to the) Tj
T*
(   comparator are POINTERS TO POINTERS \(const char **\)!) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(   2. Complete ANSI C Source Code:) Tj
T*
(   #include <stdio.h>) Tj
T*
(   #include <stdlib.h>) Tj
T*
(   #include <string.h>) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(   int compare_strings\(const void *a, const void *b\) {) Tj
T*
(   /* Dereference once to get the underlying char* string pointers */) Tj
T*
(   const char *strA = *\(const char **\)a;) Tj
T*
(   const char *strB = *\(const char **\)b;) Tj
T*
(   return strcmp\(strA, strB\);) Tj
T*
(   }) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
