(   [Problem Statement]: Explain pointer type casting and aliasing rules, detailing strict aliasing violations and the char* exception in ANSI C.) Tj
T*
(   [Detailed Step-by-Step Answer]:) Tj
T*
(   Strict Aliasing Rules and Type Punning in C:) Tj
T*
(   1. Strict Aliasing Rule \(ISO C99\):) Tj
T*
(   Compilers assume that pointers of different types \(e.g. int* and float*\) never point to the) Tj
T*
(   same memory location.) Tj
T*
(   Allowing the compiler to assume no pointer aliasing enables heavy register caching and) Tj
T*
(   reordering.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(   2. Strict Aliasing Violation:) Tj
T*
(   float f = 5.0f;) Tj
T*
(   int *ip = \(int *\)&f; /* VIOLATES STRICT ALIASING! */) Tj
T*
(   *ip = 0; /* Undefined behavior! Optimizing compiler may eliminate or reorder */) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(   3. The Universal char* Exception:) Tj
T*
(   The C standard explicitly grants an exception to character pointers \(char*, unsigned char*\):) Tj
T*
(   ANY DATA TYPE MAY BE ACCESSED AND INSPECTED BYTE-BY-BYTE THROUGH A CHARACTER POINTER!) Tj
T*
(   This exception permits memcpy\(\) and serialization engines to operate universally.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(--------------------------------------------------------------------------------) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
